From: Dustin Kirkland <dustin.kirkland@chainguard.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] logging_unittest: use a fake mailer that drains its input

The EmailLogging tests set FLAGS_logmailer to /usr/bin/true. SendEmail()
popen()s the mailer, fwrite()s the message body into the pipe and then
pclose()s it. true exits without reading its input, so when it has
already exited by the time the body is flushed the write hits a pipe
with no reader and logging_unittest dies with SIGPIPE. This is
intermittent (about 5 in 100 runs on aarch64, more likely on 1 CPU).

Use a small fake mailer script under FLAGS_test_tmpdir that ignores its
arguments and runs "cat >/dev/null", so the write always has a reader.
FLAGS_logmailer is shell-escaped as a single word by SendEmail(), so a
"sh -c ..." string cannot be used directly.

Test-only: src/logging_unittest.cc is not part of the installed library.
google/glog is archived (2025-06-30); no upstream or distro fix exists.
---
--- a/src/logging_unittest.cc
+++ b/src/logging_unittest.cc
@@ -1542,9 +1542,28 @@ TEST(LogMsgTime, gmtoff) {
   EXPECT_TRUE((gmtoff >= utc_min_offset) && (gmtoff <= utc_max_offset));
 }
 
+// A fake mailer for the EmailLogging tests. SendEmail() popen()s the mailer
+// and fwrite()s the message body into the pipe before pclose(). /usr/bin/true
+// exits without reading its input, so when it has already exited the write
+// hits a pipe with no reader and the test dies with SIGPIPE (intermittent,
+// more likely on a single CPU). This mailer ignores its arguments and drains
+// its input, so the write always has a reader.
+static const string& FakeMailer() {
+  static const string path = [] {
+    const string p = FLAGS_test_tmpdir + "/logging_unittest_fake_mailer";
+    {
+      std::ofstream out(p.c_str(), std::ios::out | std::ios::trunc);
+      out << "#!/bin/sh\ncat >/dev/null\n";
+    }
+    CHECK_EQ(chmod(p.c_str(), 0755), 0);
+    return p;
+  }();
+  return path;
+}
+
 TEST(EmailLogging, ValidAddress) {
   FlagSaver saver;
-  FLAGS_logmailer = "/usr/bin/true";
+  FLAGS_logmailer = FakeMailer();
 
   EXPECT_TRUE(
       SendEmail("example@example.com", "Example subject", "Example body"));
@@ -1552,7 +1571,7 @@ TEST(EmailLogging, ValidAddress) {
 
 TEST(EmailLogging, MultipleAddresses) {
   FlagSaver saver;
-  FLAGS_logmailer = "/usr/bin/true";
+  FLAGS_logmailer = FakeMailer();
 
   EXPECT_TRUE(SendEmail("example@example.com,foo@bar.com", "Example subject",
                         "Example body"));
@@ -1560,14 +1579,14 @@ TEST(EmailLogging, MultipleAddresses) {
 
 TEST(EmailLogging, InvalidAddress) {
   FlagSaver saver;
-  FLAGS_logmailer = "/usr/bin/true";
+  FLAGS_logmailer = FakeMailer();
 
   EXPECT_FALSE(SendEmail("hello world@foo", "Example subject", "Example body"));
 }
 
 TEST(EmailLogging, MaliciousAddress) {
   FlagSaver saver;
-  FLAGS_logmailer = "/usr/bin/true";
+  FLAGS_logmailer = FakeMailer();
 
   EXPECT_FALSE(
       SendEmail("!/bin/true@example.com", "Example subject", "Example body"));
